{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:84a51cc8aaa9caf2b358b39ab87f6d120a1b3f8f3acb97f7eafbcc51d3929b78","title":"Can primordial inflation produce the observed perturbations while ending in an intermediate-string-scale vacuum with low-energy supersymmetry? The paper assumes an answer exists and restricts its calculations to subsequent evolution.","connectionCount":0,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8472a18f77b875cdb0cfef4a80818e294fedc2e1c800372a5c6813eaf7bf4f50","title":"Review whether gravity with independently varied metric and connection can explain cosmic acceleration, satisfy local and stellar tests, admit a satisfactory initial-value formulation, and describe nonsingular high-density cosmology.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8469be6d10d480c0190ae01b4d89d132d4796ea95f8d0fcedd85a3286734180b","title":"How does localising parallel orientifold sources change BPS domain walls obtained from smeared no-scale gauged supergravity, including flows away from the potential minimum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:842c82855220da3b40400fa7761cd0b40be78c8e59b299c9d9a4b4bd37a888fd","title":"Can massive spinning particles during inflation produce observable scalar and tensor non-Gaussianity within a controlled effective theory, and which momentum dependences reveal their masses and spins?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8450e8b2aebfabc5029d3c48c9cbafc65b9e2803a196123a8345266d5b0e6bac","title":"Can topology sums remove period symmetries in every compactification, or are independent Chern–Simons mechanisms necessary? The source also proposes examining boundary anomalies and non-abelian isometries as routes to further examples.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:84f61808155ae3b9bb82932c2a99d1d3118f95568d65aec8b50296ff7cb7ac76","title":"How does local bulk effective field theory emerge from a CFT, which CFTs support it, and where does it fail? These review lectures emphasize Lorentzian physics at fixed time and the route from quantum error correction to entanglement-wedge reconstruction.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:84ed94cc09f6a635a48a1fc95ebe96e4860c3408179d488838c1336897f47caa","title":"Can chromo-natural inflation be embedded in supergravity with controlled partner fields and consistent truncations, and can its required large axion–gauge coupling arise from another stabilized scalar rather than a large input coefficient?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:84e065fbedea1a3abd4a2696aae95dc0c7b8d11c0b515ddf38ee781c4f95a90d","title":"Can an internal compactification tower explain a large-entropy black hole tower when horizon scalar values are fixed by charges? The D0–D4 construction provides explicit horizon entropy, volume, and dilaton expressions for testing that possibility.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0049"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:845e803c48654d712dc6eaf284c0c6c1c55eb0163af14e3a57f9681214936dce","title":"Can a hidden holographic environment stabilize dark energy and inflation against Planck-scale radiative mixing, erase trans-Planckian modes, and supply an entropic criterion for cosmological evolution?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0052"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8475b88ddbe5