 electrons, and what bounds follow for separately gauged Le−Lμ and Le−Lτ interactions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0098"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:845542f00280705c18af63dc207c59ce54a84edb0a31e06689a155d8c3a43796","title":"How does chiral EFT encode QCD topology, vacuum alignment and strong CP observables, and how do axions, orientifold theories and proposed phase-alignment prescriptions modify this description?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0098"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8420abacef31caf0d4bc225d7b4d13afb25ef066b24cce9128cb46aaa79d452c","title":"Can the four-derivative string effective action simultaneously retain perturbative unitarity and interpret the Kalb–Ramond field strength as totally antisymmetric torsion after compactification, and do the additional terms materially change string-inspired running-vacuum inflation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0099"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8438fa00085f56094076a8c2b001b2f1fd8a5f40d16f91d03e053882b9b18dcc","title":"Can string theory produce late-universe dark energy as a positive cosmological constant or dynamical quintessence, and which constructions survive existence, stability and correction-control constraints?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0099"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:844c3f250d4dfcdf7339199d1d64f6fd5bb62ee605e9b1973a0b1b7788777c48","title":"Can zero-temperature scattering-amplitude positivity impose sign constraints on interaction corrections to pressure, free energy, entropy and specific heat, despite the thermal state's loss of Lorentz invariance?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0101"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:849cb0f52bdfa3b6b3a807e0b4df941793e7ffc35500bdd1628b7cbd4ca4